# Rebuildable machine caches (databases, logs) - regenerated by fha index /
# fha photoindex / fha capture / fha backup, never committed. Anchored to root
# only: the tools write .cache/ exclusively at the archive root (index.sqlite,
# photos.sqlite, capture_log.jsonl, last_backup.json) - an unanchored pattern
# would also swallow any folder that happened to share the name elsewhere in
# the tree.
#
# NOT here: notes/cooccur_dismissed.json. It looks like a cache (it is
# tool-written JSON) but it holds a human's "stop suggesting this" decisions,
# which cannot be rebuilt - so it lives under notes/ and is tracked like any
# other record (#48).
/.cache/

# Rebuildable deliverables (fha site / fha views output). Anchored to root
# only: fha site and fha views write generated/ exclusively at the archive
# root - a notes/generated/ or similar IS real archive content if a human
# ever creates one, and an unanchored pattern would silently swallow it.
/generated/

# Binary asset roots. Photos and documents can be large; consider keeping them
# on an external drive and pointing roots: in fha.yaml at that location instead.
# Comment out the lines below if you want git to track originals in this repo.
# Anchored to root only - a pattern without the leading slash matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, so unanchored `photos/` also matches
# `sources/photos/`, the SOURCE RECORDS (.md files with claims) that document
# each photo - archive data, not the binary asset it describes. See #57.
/photos/
/documents/

# Staging area - inbox/ items are processed one at a time, not version-
# controlled. Anchored to root only, same reasoning as photos/documents above:
# a sources/inbox/ or notes/inbox/ would be real content, not the staging folder.
/inbox/

# Machine-local working-copy marker (git-ignored by design - see SPEC.md §12).
# Anchored to root only - the marker is only ever written at the archive root
# (`fha working-copy on`; _lib.is_working_copy checks archive_root / 'WORKING_COPY').
/WORKING_COPY

# Backup directory created by fha update-tools. Anchored to root only - it is
# only ever written at the archive root (scaffold.py's BACKUP_DIR).
/.plaintext-backup/

# Python bytecode written by the fha tools at runtime. Left UNANCHORED on
# purpose: __pycache__/ can appear inside any vendored tools subdirectory
# (.fha/tools/__pycache__/, tools/__pycache__/, …) and *.pyc has no fixed
# home either - anchoring either pattern would leave real bytecode droppings
# tracked wherever the tools happen to run from.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
